# Candidate hypotheses for the Hallelujah piano tutorial take
# (test_results/audio/07-hallelujah-piano-tutorial_piano.wav — download your
# own copy; audio is not committed). Hand-written from long-window spectral
# inspection of 28 attacks (method + evidence:
# docs/architecture/note-description-stream.md §2 and
# libkan/tests/harmonic_probe_notes.hpp, which this file mirrors).
#
# These are HYPOTHESES, not ground truth — exactly the role the chart plays
# in the game: "these pitches are believed sounding at this attack". The
# stream measures each one (presence / cents / amplitude) and flags what the
# candidates do not explain. Use with:
#
#   kan_demo --input <wav> --instrument piano \
#            --candidates apps/kan_demo/examples/hallelujah-piano-tutorial.candidates \
#            --events out.jsonl
#
# Format: "@<onset_ms> midi midi ..." binds the list to the attack nearest
# that time; plain "midi ..." lines apply to successive attacks.
# Candidates marked (sustaining) belong to earlier attacks and are re-
# measured under the new attack — the API's still-sustaining case.

